# 🇱🇰 Local SEO Checklist — Ranking ADAM in Sri Lanka

> A comprehensive, prioritized checklist to rank **ADAM (Men's Telehealth)** locally in Sri Lanka. Items are grouped by category and ordered by impact. Issues already identified in your codebase are flagged.

---

## 1. Technical SEO (On-Site Foundation)

> [!CAUTION]
> Your site is currently **missing** `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, and structured data — these are critical baseline items.

### 1.1 Crawlability & Indexing
- [ ] **Create `robots.txt`** — Add `app/robots.ts` (Next.js route handler) allowing all crawlers and pointing to the sitemap
- [ ] **Create XML Sitemap** — Add `app/sitemap.ts` that dynamically generates URLs for all pages (`/`, `/about`, `/products/[slug]`, `/blog/[slug]`, `/sexual-health`)
- [ ] **Submit sitemap to Google Search Console** — Verify ownership and submit the generated sitemap URL
- [ ] **Submit sitemap to Bing Webmaster Tools** — Secondary but still important
- [ ] **Check for crawl errors** weekly via Search Console → Coverage report
- [ ] **Ensure all pages return 200 status** — No soft 404s
- [ ] **Canonical tags** — Add canonical URLs to every page to prevent duplicate content

### 1.2 Page Speed & Core Web Vitals
- [ ] **Run Lighthouse audit** on every page — target score ≥ 90 on Performance
- [ ] **Optimize images** — Use Next.js `<Image>` component with `priority` on above-the-fold images, use WebP/AVIF
- [ ] **Lazy load below-fold images** — Ensure images not in viewport use `loading="lazy"`
- [ ] **Minimize JavaScript bundle** — Audit with `next build --analyze` (install `@next/bundle-analyzer`)
- [ ] **Enable Gzip/Brotli compression** on the hosting provider (Vercel does this by default)
- [ ] **Set proper cache headers** for static assets
- [ ] **Reduce Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)** — Preload hero image/font
- [ ] **Reduce Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)** — Set explicit `width`/`height` on all images
- [ ] **Reduce Interaction to Next Paint (INP)** — Minimize JS blocking on user interactions

### 1.3 Mobile-First
- [ ] **Verify mobile responsiveness** on all pages (Google indexes mobile-first)
- [ ] **Test with Google Mobile-Friendly Test tool**
- [ ] **Ensure tap targets are ≥ 48px**
- [ ] **No horizontal scrolling** on any breakpoint

### 1.4 HTTPS & Security
- [ ] **Ensure HTTPS is enforced** site-wide (redirect HTTP → HTTPS)
- [ ] **HSTS header** enabled
- [ ] **No mixed content** (all resources loaded over HTTPS)

---

## 2. On-Page SEO (Content & Metadata)

> [!WARNING]
> Your root layout has a generic title `"ADAM - Men's Telehealth"` and description. Every page needs **unique, keyword-rich** metadata.

### 2.1 Metadata Per Page
| Page | Suggested Title | Suggested Description |
|------|----------------|----------------------|
| `/` (Home) | `ADAM - Men's Health & Telehealth Sri Lanka \| Hair Loss, ED & Wellness` | `Sri Lanka's leading men's telehealth platform. Online consultations with licensed Sri Lankan doctors for hair loss, ED, and wellness. Discreet & affordable.` |
| `/about` | `About ADAM \| Sri Lanka's #1 Men's Health Platform` | `Learn about ADAM's mission to provide accessible, discreet healthcare for men across Sri Lanka. Meet our team of licensed doctors.` |
| `/products/[slug]` | Dynamic: `{Product Name} \| ADAM Men's Health Sri Lanka` | Dynamic: description from product data |
| `/blog/[slug]` | Dynamic: `{Article Title} \| ADAM Health Blog` | Dynamic: first 155 chars of article |
| `/sexual-health` | `Sexual Health Solutions for Men \| ADAM Sri Lanka` | `Confidential sexual health consultations and treatments for men in Sri Lanka. FDA-approved medications. Doctor-prescribed.` |

- [ ] **Add unique `<title>` tags** to every page (50–60 chars, include "Sri Lanka")
- [ ] **Add unique `<meta description>`** to every page (150–160 chars)
- [ ] **Add Open Graph tags** (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:url`, `og:type`)
- [ ] **Add Twitter Card tags** (`twitter:card`, `twitter:title`, `twitter:description`, `twitter:image`)
- [ ] **Create a compelling OG image** (1200×630px) for social sharing

### 2.2 Heading Structure
- [ ] **One `<h1>` per page** — keyword-rich and descriptive
- [ ] **Logical heading hierarchy** — `<h1>` → `<h2>` → `<h3>`, no skipped levels
- [ ] **Include geo-modifier in at least one heading** — e.g., "Men's Health Solutions *in Sri Lanka*"

### 2.3 Content Optimization
- [ ] **Target primary keywords per page:**
  - Home: `men's health sri lanka`, `telehealth sri lanka`, `online doctor sri lanka`
  - Products: `{product name} sri lanka`, `buy {product} online sri lanka`
  - Blog: long-tail informational queries (see §6)
  - Sexual Health: `sexual health clinic sri lanka`, `ED treatment sri lanka`
- [ ] **Natural keyword density** — 1–2% for primary keyword, avoid stuffing
- [ ] **Use LSI (related) keywords** — e.g., `men's wellness`, `hair regrowth`, `testosterone`, `telehealth consultation`
- [ ] **Add alt text to ALL images** — descriptive and keyword-relevant
- [ ] **Internal linking** — Link between related pages (e.g., blog articles → product pages)
- [ ] **External links** — Link to authoritative medical sources (WHO, NIH) for trust signals

### 2.4 URL Structure
- [ ] **Clean, readable URLs** — e.g., `/products/minoxidil-5-topical-solution` not `/products/prod123`
- [ ] **Include keywords in slugs** — keep them short and descriptive
- [ ] **Lowercase URLs only**, no special characters

