## 3. Structured Data (Schema Markup)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Structured data is **completely missing** from your site. This is a huge missed opportunity for rich results.

- [ ] **Organization Schema** — Add to root layout
  ```json
  {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "ADAM",
    "url": "https://adamhealth.lk",
    "logo": "https://adamhealth.lk/logo.png",
    "sameAs": ["facebook-url", "instagram-url"],
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressCountry": "LK",
      "addressLocality": "Colombo"
    }
  }
  ```
- [ ] **MedicalBusiness / HealthAndBeautyBusiness Schema** — For local business signals
- [ ] **Product Schema** — On each product page (name, description, price, availability)
- [ ] **FAQPage Schema** — On the FAQ section (generates rich FAQ snippets in Google)
- [ ] **Article / BlogPosting Schema** — On each blog post (headline, author, datePublished, image)
- [ ] **BreadcrumbList Schema** — For navigation breadcrumbs
- [ ] **Review / AggregateRating Schema** — If you have customer reviews
- [ ] **MedicalWebPage Schema** — For health-related content pages
- [ ] **Validate all schema** with [Google Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results)

---

## 4. Locale & Language Targeting

> [!WARNING]
> Your site uses `lang="en"` but has no explicit Sri Lanka geo-targeting. Google needs stronger signals.

- [ ] **Use a `.lk` domain** (e.g., `adamhealth.lk`) — strongest geo-signal, OR:
- [ ] **Use a subdirectory** (e.g., `adam.com/lk/`) if using a generic TLD
- [ ] **Set geo-target in Google Search Console** → Settings → International Targeting → Country = Sri Lanka
- [ ] **Add `hreflang` tag**: `<link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-LK" href="https://yoursite.lk/" />`
- [ ] **Consider Sinhala/Tamil content** — Even a few key pages in Sinhala (`si`) or Tamil (`ta`) would help:
  - [ ] Add `hreflang="si-LK"` and `hreflang="ta-LK"` alternate versions
  - [ ] Target keywords in Sinhala script for low-competition wins
- [ ] **Use Sri Lankan currency (LKR)** in product pricing with proper markup
- [ ] **Sri Lankan phone number format** — Display in `+94 XX XXX XXXX` format
- [ ] **Sri Lankan address** — Display physical or registered business address on site

---

## 5. Google Business Profile (GBP) & Local Listings

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the **#1 factor** for local pack rankings (the map results).

### 5.1 Google Business Profile
- [ ] **Create/claim Google Business Profile** at [business.google.com](https://business.google.com)
- [ ] **Choose correct category**: `Telehealth Service` or `Health Consultant`
- [ ] **Add secondary categories**: `Men's Health Clinic`, `Online Pharmacy`
- [ ] **Complete ALL profile fields**:
  - Business name (exact match to website)
  - Address (if you have a physical location)
  - Service areas (Colombo, Kandy, Galle, etc.)
  - Phone number
  - Website URL
  - Business hours
  - Business description (750 chars, keyword-rich)
- [ ] **Upload high-quality photos** — logo, team, office, products (minimum 10 photos)
- [ ] **Add all services** with descriptions
- [ ] **Enable messaging**
- [ ] **Post weekly Google Business updates** (offers, health tips, new products)
- [ ] **Respond to ALL reviews** within 24 hours

### 5.2 Local Citations & Directories (Sri Lanka-Specific)
- [ ] **List on Sri Lankan business directories**:
  - [LankaBusinessOnline.com](https://lankabusinessonline.com)
  - [Cylex.lk](https://www.cylex.lk)
  - [BusinessList.lk](https://businesslist.lk)
  - [YellowPages.lk](https://www.yellowpages.lk)
  - [Srilankabusiness.com](https://srilankabusiness.com)
- [ ] **List on healthcare-specific directories**:
  - [Doctorlk.com](https://doctorlk.com)
  - [HealthNet.lk](https://healthnet.lk)
- [ ] **List on global directories**:
  - Yelp, Bing Places, Apple Maps, Facebook Business Page
- [ ] **Ensure NAP consistency** — Name, Address, Phone must be **identical** across ALL listings

---

## 6. Content Strategy (Blog & Topical Authority)

> [!TIP]
> Consistent, high-quality blog content is your biggest lever for long-tail traffic in Sri Lanka, where competition is relatively low.

### 6.1 Keyword Research (Sri Lanka Focus)
- [ ] **Research keywords using**:
  - Google Keyword Planner (set location to Sri Lanka)
  - Ubersuggest (filter by LK)
  - AnswerThePublic
  - Google Trends (filter by Sri Lanka)
  - "People Also Ask" boxes for Sri Lankan queries
- [ ] **Target question-based keywords** — these often have zero competition in LK:
  - "best hair loss treatment in Sri Lanka"
  - "online doctor consultation Sri Lanka"
  - "is telehealth available in Sri Lanka"
  - "ED treatment price Sri Lanka"
  - "men's health clinic Colombo"
  - "hair regrowth treatment cost Sri Lanka"

### 6.2 Content Calendar
- [ ] **Publish 2–4 blog posts per month** minimum
- [ ] **Mix content types**:
  - Informational: "How does minoxidil work?"
  - Local: "Best men's health clinics in Colombo"
  - Comparison: "Telehealth vs in-person doctor visits in Sri Lanka"
  - Guide: "Complete guide to treating hair loss in Sri Lanka"
  - FAQ: "Is online prescription legal in Sri Lanka?"
- [ ] **Create pillar pages** — comprehensive guides (2000+ words) for each main topic:
  - Pillar: "Men's Hair Loss in Sri Lanka" → links to 10+ supporting blog posts
  - Pillar: "Men's Sexual Health Guide" → links to treatments, FAQs, doctor info
- [ ] **Add a dedicated FAQ page** `/faq` with common questions (great for featured snippets)

### 6.3 Content Quality
- [ ] **E-E-A-T compliance** (Experience, Expertise, Authority, Trust):
  - [ ] Author bio with medical credentials on every blog post
  - [ ] "Medically reviewed by Dr. [Name]" badges
  - [ ] Link to doctor's credentials/license verification
  - [ ] Cite peer-reviewed sources
- [ ] **Add a "Medical Disclaimer"** page
- [ ] **Add "About Our Doctors"** page with full bios, photos, credentials
- [ ] **Add a "Privacy Policy"** and **"Terms of Service"** page

